== 12. Advancement <core-advancement>
#columns(2, gutter: 6mm)[
// PLAYTEST: milestone definition
A #strong[milestone] is the end of a story arc or the completion of a major Goal; the GM calls it, usually at the end of a session. A #strong[major milestone] is the end of a full campaign arc. (Playtest Value)

=== 12.1 Earning XP (end of session) <core-earning-xp>
1 XP per "yes" unless noted:

- Did you hit your #strong[playbook XP trigger]? (1, or 2 in a scene with lethal stakes or a listed Danger, @core-dangers-conflicts)
- Did you #strong[accomplish your Goal]? (+2)
- Did one or more of your #strong[World, Other, or Self Beliefs] drive a meaningful decision?
- Did your #strong[Instinct] get you into trouble or save the day?
- Did you face consequences from a #strong[compelled tag or Scar]?

The Belief question awards at most #strong[1 XP per session], not 1 XP per Belief. Upholding, questioning, or acting against a Belief can qualify when it drives a meaningful decision; merely reciting or rewriting it does not.

#strong[MVP vote:] the table votes on one standout moment each session; that player gets +1 Tychē Point at the next session (above Refresh, within the cap).

=== 12.2 Spending XP (every 6 XP = 1 Advance) <core-spending-xp>
- +1 to a skill (following the pyramid rule)
- +3 to one pool, or +1 Edge (max 3 Edge per pool)
- A new playbook special ability (★ costs 1 Refresh; veteran costs below)
- A new tag, or rewrite an existing tag
- A new Specialisation in a rated skill (@core-skill-pyramid)
- #strong[+1 Refresh] (buys back Refresh spent on abilities or artifacts), up to the #strong[Refresh cap] of 3 + 1 per 3 Advances
- A higher-tier Focus ability: Tier 2 after 3 Advances; Tier 3 after 6 Advances. Taking the ability costs an Advance; reaching the threshold does not grant it automatically (Generic Focuses @foc-what-focus-gives-you).
- #strong[+1 Effort Level] (to Level 2 after 3 Advances; Level 3 after 9 Advances)
- #strong[Quick Recovery] (once only): recover 1 additional point on every recovery roll. It doesn't change the fourth rest's full recovery (@core-rest-recovery).

#strong[Focus choices.] Tier 1 is gained at creation. At Tiers 2 and 3, choose one of the tier's two options when buying that ability. Once eligible for the tier, its unchosen option can be taken later as a normal Advance. A ★ option also costs 1 Refresh.

#strong[Veteran abilities.] After 6 Advances, you may take an ability from another playbook as an Advance. It costs 1 Refresh plus any ★ cost, so a veteran ★ costs 2 Refresh (Generic Playbooks @pb-ability-notation).

#strong[Capstones.] A capstone unlocks after 12 Advances if you have at least 4 abilities from that playbook. Take it as an Advance; it costs no Refresh, and a character can have only one.

#strong[Refresh limits.] Purchases can't take Refresh below 1 (@core-refresh) or above the Refresh cap.

=== 12.3 Reviewing Beliefs and Instincts <core-reviewing-beliefs-instincts>
Review the relevance of your Beliefs at session end. Ask:

#quote(block: true)[Which conviction did events reinforce, complicate, or overturn?]

Use the answer to review your World, Other and Self Beliefs. A conviction may stay firm, grow more complicated or stop fitting the character; you don't have to change a Belief because you questioned or acted against it. The question is a reflection prompt, not a reward: answering it earns nothing by itself (@core-earning-xp).

Ordinary revisions happen at milestones. Reaffirm, revise, or replace your Beliefs to reflect development in play.

- #strong[Reaffirm:] keep a conviction and commitment that still matter.
- #strong[Revise:] update a fulfilled or obsolete action clause while keeping the underlying conviction.
#colbreak()
- #strong[Replace:] write a new Belief when experience changes your outlook or the former commitment no longer belongs in the campaign.
- #strong[Relationships:] review an Other Belief when the relationship meaningfully changes; agree on shared premises with the other player as in @core-beliefs-goals-instincts.

Acting against a Belief has no automatic penalty and doesn't force a rewrite; the player decides whether it leads to reaffirmation or change. Don't rewrite a Belief mid-decision to claim a reward. Rewriting alone earns neither XP nor Tychē.

Keep one World, one Other and one Self Belief. Rewrite a Goal when it's accomplished or no longer fits (@core-beliefs-goals-instincts). Instincts can change at milestones.
]
